{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_settings_settings_panel", "label": "The Settings panel, section by section", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L1-10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything the console lets you change about itself, in one panel. It replaced the modals that used to hang off the chips in the top strip and the About page with them. Opened with the gear or S; the link chip goes to Robot with the team field focused, L to Dashboard, and the wordmark, ? and F1 to About."}, {"id": "docs_settings_nothing_applies", "label": "Nothing applies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L14-16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no apply button and no confirmation step, because a control is the truth the moment you move it. The surface that changed a setting is responsible for making the board agree with it, and does so immediately."}, {"id": "docs_settings_nothing_is_modal", "label": "Nothing is modal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L18-20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No focus trap, no inert dashboard behind it, and the markup does not claim otherwise. It is a mode you step out of rather than a window that holds you \u2014 claiming modality would have been the markup saying one thing while the program did another."}, {"id": "docs_settings_it_stands_down", "label": "It stands down", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L22-24", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The moment the robot is enabled or E-stopped the panel closes itself along with anything else covering the board. Rule two: a driver who opened Settings in the pit and then got called to the field must not find the state lamp, the match timer and the E-stop indicator behind a panel."}, {"id": "docs_settings_search_in_place", "label": "Searching leaves matches where they live", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L26-43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing is cloned into a results list \u2014 the row you find is the row itself, with the handler it was built with. The label, its explanation and any text on the control are all searched, so 'inches' finds Units, whose own word is 'Imperial'. A query that matches nothing says so, quoting what you typed. Escape clears the filter; a second Escape closes the panel. About holds prose rather than rows, so it never matches and never claims to."}, {"id": "docs_settings_devices_section", "label": "The Devices section", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L62-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sheet answers what is this robot; this answers what is on it and where, which is a different question asked at a different time. CAN devices as a tree, one group per bus, needing FrcCatalyst 1.12+ which publishes Hardware/Devices as bus|id|type. Neither half is a setting, so neither is reachable by search."}, {"id": "docs_settings_power_panel_needs_a_count", "label": "The power board is drawn only from a published channel count", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L73-75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It appears only when the robot published a channel count \u2014 a strip sized to whatever happens to be in use would be inventing the shape of a distribution board nobody described. Rule 3 applied to a drawing rather than to a number."}, {"id": "docs_settings_trail_length_rebuild", "label": "Trail length applies on release", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L87", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applied on release rather than during the drag, because the trail buffer is allocated when the scene is built, so changing the length is a rebuild."}, {"id": "docs_settings_one_camera_two_surfaces", "label": "One camera, two surfaces, one function", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L86", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The buttons in the tile's own corner move the same setting as the Settings row; there is one camera and both surfaces go through one function to change it, because a tile quietly holding a camera of its own is how the two came to disagree."}, {"id": "docs_settings_opens_on_applies_at_launch", "label": "Opens on applies at launch only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L96", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Setting it does not switch the view now, because that would be the setting acting on the wrong occasion."}, {"id": "docs_settings_import_checked_whole", "label": "An import is checked whole before anything is applied", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L98", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A document with one bad tile is refused with the reason, and the board on screen is left alone. A half-applied layout would be worse than a refused one."}, {"id": "docs_settings_reset_arms_itself", "label": "Reset arms itself rather than opening a dialog", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two presses rather than a dialog \u2014 the button arms itself and disarms after four seconds \u2014 because rule two says nothing blocks the board."}, {"id": "docs_settings_alert_hold", "label": "Alert hold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L101", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "How long a cleared alert stays on screen, dimmed, 0 to 8 s. Applied live on the drag since nothing has to be rebuilt. Robot alerts sitting near their threshold raise and clear repeatedly, and a tile that strobes next to a driver is worse than useless."}, {"id": "docs_settings_demo_is_amber", "label": "Demo data is amber, alone among the switches", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L112-119", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Off by default and never remembered, the dock button stays lit the whole time it runs, and switching it on stands this panel down exactly as a robot enabling does. A dashboard that quietly invents telemetry is a hazard, so every part of that is deliberate. The duplicate switch in the dock is on purpose: while demo runs the fact that the numbers are invented has to be visible on the dashboard itself."}, {"id": "docs_settings_release_notes_as_plain_text", "label": "Release notes are shown as plain text, never rendered", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L130-132", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The notes are shown before you decide rather than after \u2014 the page is a decision rather than a changelog. The text arrived over the network, so it is shown as plain text and never rendered as markup."}, {"id": "docs_settings_about_reads_across", "label": "About lays the three rules across on a wide window", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L142-147", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On a window 1080px or wider the three rules sit side by side rather than stacked, so they are read across rather than scrolled through: they are one idea in three parts, and a reader who has to scroll to reach the third has stopped holding the first two. Narrower than that it folds back to one column."}, {"id": "docs_settings_frames_counts_real_ones", "label": "Frames counts real NetworkTables frames only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L149-152", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Demo ticks are not NetworkTables frames, and counting them would be the console inventing a number about itself. Rule 3 turned inward on the console's own diagnostics."}, {"id": "docs_settings_bundled_versus_switched_off", "label": "Bundled but switched off says exactly that", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L154-156", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A model that is bundled but switched off reports itself as such, rather than reporting a preference as a fact about the build."}, {"id": "docs_settings_single_key_bindings", "label": "Every binding is a single unmodified key", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L158-174", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A driver station is operated under pressure and often without looking down. That is exactly why typing in any field suspends them all: a bare d must never toggle demo data while somebody is halfway through typing a topic path. Escape in a field means abandon what I am typing and blurs it; a second Escape closes what is open."}, {"id": "docs_settings_storage_checked_key_by_key", "label": "Storage is read one key at a time and every key is checked", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L176-184", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A number outside its range is pulled back into it and anything else falls back to the default, because storage can hold anything \u2014 an older build wrote it, someone edited it by hand, a quota error truncated it \u2014 and a bad value out of there lands in a component that has no business validating a setting. Everything lives in local storage except the team number, which belongs to the backend because the MCP server has to read it with no webview involved."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_settings_settings_panel", "target": "readme_settings_panel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L1-10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_app_buildsettings", "target": "docs_settings_settings_panel", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L1-10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_app_paintsettings", "target": "docs_settings_settings_panel", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L1-10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_app_showsection", "target": "docs_settings_settings_panel", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L7-10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_settings_nothing_applies", "target": "readme_settings_panel", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/settings.md", "source_location": "L14-16", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_settings_nothing_is_modal", "target": "readme_rule_2_never_impedes_driving", "relation": "implements", "confide